---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { directions } from "../../directions.mjs";

const swatchRoles = ["--bg", "--surface", "--border", "--accent", "--ok", "--warn", "--danger"];
const switcherSample = `const slugs = [${directions.map((d) => JSON.stringify(d.slug)).join(", ")}];
const saved = localStorage.getItem("uiforagents-direction");
document.documentElement.dataset.theme = slugs.includes(saved) ? saved : "midnight";
const switcher = document.querySelector("[data-direction-switcher]");
switcher.value = document.documentElement.dataset.theme;
switcher.addEventListener("change", () => {
  document.documentElement.dataset.theme = switcher.value;
  localStorage.setItem("uiforagents-direction", switcher.value);
});`;
---
<Base title="Theming - uiforagents">
  <div class="page">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1>Theming</h1>
      <p>The kit's components read semantic roles - <code>--bg</code>, <code>--surface</code>, <code>--accent</code>, status triplets - never colors. A <strong>direction</strong> is a complete token set for those roles: palette, radius, shadow character, type pairing, density. Swap the direction and every component restyles, with no per-component overrides anywhere.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="catalog-section">
      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <p>The site ships tokens.css with all {directions.length} directions bundled: a <code>:root</code> fallback plus one <code>[data-theme]</code> block per direction. The switcher script applies your persisted choice to <code>document.documentElement.dataset.theme</code> before first paint, so there is no flash and no server state - one vanilla recipe, ~10 lines.</p>
      <div class="uif-code-block">
        <div data-slot="header">
          <span data-slot="label">switcher.js</span>
          <button type="button" data-slot="copy">Copy</button>
        </div>
        <pre data-slot="code"><code>{switcherSample}</code></pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="catalog-section">
      <h2>The directions</h2>
      <p>Curated in the lab's direction library and sampled side by side before this site picked its
      default (<strong>Midnight</strong>). Click a card to apply it site-wide; the switcher keeps it.</p>
      <div class="direction-grid">
        {directions.map((d) => (
          <button type="button" class="direction-card" data-apply-direction={d.slug} aria-label={`Apply the ${d.name} direction`}>
            <span class="direction-swatches">
              {swatchRoles.map((role) => (
                <span style={`background: ${d.tokens[role]};`}></span>
              ))}
            </span>
            <span class="direction-card-body">
              <h2>{d.name}</h2>
              <p>{d.mood} · {d.notes}</p>
              <span class="direction-state" data-direction-state={d.slug}></span>
            </span>
          </button>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
